# Merged into agent/scripts/ from backend/agent-runtime/automaton-agent.service
# as part of the agent-runtime -> agent merge (see /MERGE-NOTES.md).
#
# NOTE: this unit was already marked DEPRECATED in agent-runtime (see the
# body below) in favor of backend/src/orchestrator.ts's spawn/kill admin
# endpoints. That orchestrator lives in the separate automaton-backend
# project, not in this agent/ repo, so those endpoints aren't reachable
# from here. Kept for the same reason the original kept it: history and
# reference, not a deployment recommendation. Left fully commented out,
# unchanged from the original.

# /etc/systemd/system/automaton-agent.service
#
# next-phase.md Phase 5a (architecture-agent.md §6, The Orchestrator):
# DEPRECATED. This unit used to be the singleton launcher for this
# package's dist/index.js — exactly one agent process, ever, with no
# process-level notion of *which* agent it was beyond whatever env vars
# happened to be in EnvironmentFile. That assumption is what Phase 5a
# replaces: every top-level agent this backend knows about (the founder
# and every Phase 4 clone()) now gets spawned and killed independently
# by backend/src/orchestrator.ts, via:
#
#   POST /admin/orchestrator/:address/spawn   (x-admin-key required)
#   POST /admin/orchestrator/:address/kill    (x-admin-key required)
#   GET  /admin/orchestrator/:address/status
#   GET  /admin/orchestrator/processes
#
# instead of systemd managing one hardcoded instance. Do not install or
# enable this unit for new deployments — start automaton-backend.service
# (which stays a normal singleton systemd unit; there is only ever one
# backend) and use the endpoints above to bring up agent processes.
#
# Left in the repo, deprecated rather than deleted, for two reasons:
#   1. A reader following the pre-Phase-5a docs/history to this path
#      should find an explanation, not a broken reference — the same
#      "pointer, not a gap" convention next-phase.md's own header
#      comments use elsewhere (e.g. Phase 4c's erc8004Trust.ts note).
#   2. Process-level restart-on-crash (Restart=on-failure below) is a
#      real capability this unit had that orchestrator.ts's Phase 5a
#      spawn/kill primitives do NOT yet reproduce — that's Phase 5e
#      (health-check + auto-restart)'s explicit job, not this phase's.
#      Until 5e ships, a spawned agent process that crashes stays
#      crashed (correctly reported via GET .../status) until an
#      operator calls POST .../spawn again by hand.
#
# [Unit]
# Description=Automaton agent runtime (superseded by orchestrator.ts — see above)
# After=network.target automaton-backend.service
# Wants=automaton-backend.service
#
# [Service]
# Type=simple
# User=automaton
# WorkingDirectory=/opt/automaton-backend/agent-runtime
# EnvironmentFile=/opt/automaton-backend/agent-runtime/.env
# ExecStart=/usr/bin/node dist/index.js
# Restart=on-failure
# RestartSec=30
#
# [Install]
# WantedBy=multi-user.target
